    "sys.path.append(os.path.abspath('../src'))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visual formatting\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10, 6)\n",
    "plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 11\n",
    "os.makedirs('../docs', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs('../data', exist_ok=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Part 1: Business Framing & Exploratory Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "### Load Dataset\n",
    "Downloading IBM Telco Customer Churn dataset dynamically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DATA_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IBM/telco-customer-churn-on-icp-for-data/master/data/Telco-Customer-Churn.csv\"\n",
    "DATA_PATH = \"../data/Telco-Customer-Churn.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(DATA_PATH):\n",
    "    print(\"Downloading dataset...\")\n",
    "    df_raw = pd.read_csv(DATA_URL)\n",
    "    df_raw.to_csv(DATA_PATH, index=False)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    df_raw = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset Shape: {df_raw.shape}\")\n",
    "df_raw.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Core KPIs & Breakdown"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compute overall churn rate\n",
    "df_raw['ChurnBinary'] = df_raw['Churn'].map({'Yes': 1, 'No': 0})\n",
    "overall_churn_rate = df_raw['ChurnBinary'].mean() * 100\n",
    "print(f\"Overall Churn Rate: {overall_churn_rate:.2f}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Churn breakdown by Contract type\n",
    "contract_churn = df_raw.groupby('Contract')['ChurnBinary'].agg(['count', 'mean']).reset_index()\n",
    "contract_churn['churn_pct'] = contract_churn['mean'] * 100\n",
    "print(\"\\nChurn Rate by Contract Type:\")\n",
    "print(contract_churn[['Contract', 'count', 'churn_pct']])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Churn breakdown by Internet Service\n",
    "internet_churn = df_raw.groupby('InternetService')['ChurnBinary'].agg(['count', 'mean']).reset_index()\n",
    "internet_churn['churn_pct'] = internet_churn['mean'] * 100\n",
    "print(\"\\nChurn Rate by Internet Service:\")\n",
    "print(internet_churn[['InternetService', 'count', 'churn_pct']])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Visualization: Tenure vs Churn"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "sns.kdeplot(data=df_raw, x='tenure', hue='Churn', common_norm=False, fill=True, palette=['#2ec4b6', '#e71d36'])\n",
    "plt.title('Tenure Distribution by Churn Status', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Tenure (Months)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Density')\n",
    "plt.savefig('../docs/tenure_vs_churn.png', bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Analytical Questions (Part 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q1: Why is Contract Type correlation, not causation?**  \n",
    "* **Self-Selection Bias:** Customers who plan to stay long-term actively self-select into 1-year or 2-year contracts to secure lower monthly rates. Conversely, customers with uncertain needs or high price sensitivity opt for month-to-month contracts so they can leave at any time.\n",
    "* **Operational Implication:** Forcing high-risk month-to-month customers into long-term contracts without addressing core dissatisfaction drivers (e.g., service quality or pricing) will lead to early cancellations or refusal to renew rather than genuine retention."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Part 2: Predictive Modelling & Business Segmentation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Cleaning & Governance Rules"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Fix TotalCharges column\n",
    "df_clean = df_raw.copy()\n",
    "df_clean['TotalCharges'] = pd.to_numeric(df_clean['TotalCharges'].str.strip(), errors='coerce')\n",
    "df_clean['TotalCharges'].fillna(df_clean['MonthlyCharges'], inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Governance Policy Implementation\n",
    "# Protected demographics are retained for audit analysis but removed from model training features\n",
    "PROTECTED_DEMOGRAPHICS = ['gender', 'SeniorCitizen', 'Partner', 'Dependents']\n",
    "EXCLUDE_COLS = ['customerID', 'Churn', 'ChurnBinary'] + PROTECTED_DEMOGRAPHICS\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_cols = [c for c in df_clean.columns if c not in EXCLUDE_COLS]\n",
    "X = df_clean[feature_cols]\n",
    "y = df_clean['ChurnBinary']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Features used for model training ({len(feature_cols)}): {feature_cols}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Train/Test Split & Preprocessing Pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=42, stratify=y)\n",
    "\n",
    "num_cols = X.select_dtypes(include=['int64', 'float64']).columns.tolist()\n",
    "cat_cols = X.select_dtypes(include=['object']).columns.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
    "    transformers=[\n",
    "        ('num', StandardScaler(), num_cols),\n",
    "        ('cat', OneHotEncoder(drop='first', handle_unknown='ignore'), cat_cols)\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_prep = preprocessor.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_prep = preprocessor.transform(X_test)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Model Training & Evaluation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Logistic Regression Baseline\n",
    "lr = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=42)\n",
    "lr.fit(X_train_prep, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred_lr = lr.predict(X_test_prep)\n",
    "y_proba_lr = lr.predict_proba(X_test_prep)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Random Forest Classifier (Optimized for Recall/Generalization)\n",
    "rf = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, max_depth=8, class_weight='balanced', random_state=42)\n",
    "rf.fit(X_train_prep, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred_rf = rf.predict(X_test_prep)\n",
    "y_proba_rf = rf.predict_proba(X_test_prep)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Overfitting Diagnostic\n",
    "rf_train_acc = accuracy_score(y_train, rf.predict(X_train_prep))\n",
    "rf_test_acc = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred_rf)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"=== Random Forest Performance ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Train Accuracy: {rf_train_acc*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test Accuracy:  {rf_test_acc*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy Gap:   {(rf_train_acc - rf_test_acc)*100:.2f} percentage points\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test Recall:    {recall_score(y_test, y_pred_rf)*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test Precision: {precision_score(y_test, y_pred_rf)*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test ROC-AUC:   {roc_auc_score(y_test, y_proba_rf):.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Feature Importance Signals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ohe_cols = preprocessor.named_transformers_['cat'].get_feature_names_out(cat_cols)\n",
    "all_feature_names = num_cols + list(ohe_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "importances = pd.Series(rf.feature_importances_, index=all_feature_names).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "importances.head(10).plot(kind='barh', color='#2b5c8f')\n",
    "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
    "plt.title('Top 10 Feature Importances (Random Forest)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Relative Importance')\n",
    "plt.savefig('../docs/feature_importance.png', bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Top 3 Global Feature Signals:\")\n",
    "for idx, (name, val) in enumerate(importances.head(3).items(), 1):\n",
    "    print(f\"{idx}. {name}: {val:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Customer Segmentation & Revenue Risk"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get full dataset predictions for segmentation\n",
    "X_full_prep = preprocessor.transform(X)\n",
    "df_clean['predicted_churn_prob'] = rf.predict_proba(X_full_prep)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Business Segmentation Logic\n",
    "def segment_customer(row):\n",
    "    is_new = row['tenure'] < 12\n",
    "    is_high_spend = row['MonthlyCharges'] >= 65.0\n",
    "    is_high_risk = row['predicted_churn_prob'] >= 0.50\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if is_new and is_high_spend and is_high_risk:\n",
    "        return 'New, high-spend, high-risk'\n",
    "    elif not is_new and is_high_spend and not is_high_risk:\n",
    "        return 'Established, high-spend, low-risk'\n",
    "    elif is_new and not is_high_spend and is_high_risk:\n",
    "        return 'New, low-spend, high-risk'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'Established, low-spend, low-risk'\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean['segment'] = df_clean.apply(segment_customer, axis=1)\n",
    "df_clean['expected_monthly_loss'] = df_clean['MonthlyCharges'] * df_clean['predicted_churn_prob']\n",
    "\n",
    "segment_summary = df_clean.groupby('segment').agg(\n",
    "    customer_count=('customerID', 'count'),\n",
    "    avg_monthly_charges=('MonthlyCharges', 'mean'),\n",
    "    avg_churn_risk=('predicted_churn_prob', 'mean'),\n",
    "    total_expected_revenue_at_risk=('expected_monthly_loss', 'sum')\n",
    ").reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(segment_summary.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Analytical Questions (Part 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q2A: Why accuracy alone is misleading for minority classes**  \n",
    "In imbalanced datasets (e.g., 26.5% churn), a naive model predicting \"No Churn\" for everyone achieves 73.5% accuracy but catches 0% of churners. For retention teams, **Recall** is the critical metric because missing a churner costs lifetime customer value, whereas a false alarm only costs a small discount.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q2B: How to diagnose overfitting**  \n",
    "Overfitting occurs when a model learns training noise rather than true underlying patterns. A 14.99 percentage point gap between train accuracy (~91%) and test accuracy (~76%) indicates generalization risk. This is mitigated using tree depth restrictions (`max_depth=8`) and cross-validation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Part 3: GenAI Advisory Layer — Prompt Engineering & RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "### Rule-Based Playbook & Retriever (No Vector DB Required)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PLAYBOOK = {\n",
    "    \"Clause_1\": \"High Risk (>=70%): Offer immediate 15% loyalty discount on 1-year renewal and schedule a priority 48-hour callback from customer success.\",\n",
    "    \"Clause_2\": \"Moderate Risk (40-60%): Send targeted feature discovery email highlighting unutilized premium services and offer a 10% plan upgrade bonus.\",\n",
    "    \"Clause_3\": \"New Customer (<3 months): Route immediately to specialized onboarding team for personal account setup and service walk-through.\",\n",
    "    \"Clause_4\": \"Non-Discrimination Policy: Strictly forbid referencing gender, age, marital status, or dependent status in retention rationale or offers.\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def retrieve_playbook_clause(churn_prob, tenure_months):\n",
    "    # Standardized retrieval rule\n",
    "    clauses = []\n",
    "    if tenure_months < 3:\n",
    "        clauses.append(PLAYBOOK[\"Clause_3\"])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if churn_prob >= 0.70:\n",
    "        clauses.append(PLAYBOOK[\"Clause_1\"])\n",
    "    elif 0.40 <= churn_prob < 0.70:\n",
    "        clauses.append(PLAYBOOK[\"Clause_2\"])\n",
    "        \n",
    "    clauses.append(PLAYBOOK[\"Clause_4\"]) # Governance clause always appended\n",
    "    return \" \\n\".join(clauses)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example retrieval test\n",
    "sample_clause = retrieve_playbook_clause(0.76, 2)\n",
    "print(\"Retrieved Playbook Guidance:\\n\", sample_clause)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Grounded Prompt Design & Compliance Guardrails"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def construct_retention_prompt(customer_id, risk_prob, tenure, monthly_charges, top_signals, retrieved_clause):\n",
    "    prompt = f\"\"\"\n",
    "You are an executive retention advisor for a telecom company.\n",
    "Generate a professional, compliant retention recommendation for Customer ID: {customer_id}.\n",
    "\n",
    "CUSTOMER CONTEXT:\n",
    "- Predicted Churn Risk: {risk_prob*100:.1f}%\n",
    "- Tenure: {tenure} months\n",
    "- Monthly Spend: ${monthly_charges:.2f}\n",
    "- Key Operational Signals: {', '.join(top_signals)}\n",
    "\n",
    "APPROVED RETENTION PLAYBOOK CLAUSES:\n",
    "{retrieved_clause}\n",
    "\n",
    "STRICT COMPLIANCE DIRECTIVES:\n",
    "1. Rely ONLY on the provided retention playbook clauses.\n",
    "2. NEVER mention protected attributes (gender, age, partner, dependents).\n",
    "3. Format response in 3 concise bullet points: Risk Assessment, Approved Action, Talking Points.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "    return prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "sample_prompt = construct_retention_prompt(\n",
    "    customer_id=\"1234-ABCD\",\n",
    "    risk_prob=0.764,\n",
    "    tenure=2,\n",
    "    monthly_charges=79.14,\n",
    "    top_signals=[\"Tenure\", \"TotalCharges\", \"Month-to-month contract\"],\n",
    "    retrieved_clause=sample_clause\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(sample_prompt)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Automated Compliance Validator"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def validate_llm_response(response_text):\n",
    "    BANNED_TERMS = ['gender', 'female', 'male', 'senior', 'age', 'old', 'partner', 'married', 'dependents', 'children', 'family']\n",
    "    violations = [term for term in BANNED_TERMS if term in response_text.lower()]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    is_compliant = len(violations) == 0\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"is_compliant\": is_compliant,\n",
    "        \"violations_found\": violations\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test validator against synthetic non-compliant text\n",
    "test_text = \"Customer is high risk because she is a senior citizen with no partner.\"\n",
    "print(\"Validation Test Result:\", validate_llm_response(test_text))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Analytical Questions (Part 3)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q3A: Hallucination in Compliance Contexts**  \n",
    "Hallucination occurs when an LLM invents unauthorized discounts or unapproved retention promises. In regulated customer communications, this creates binding legal risks, margin erosion, and brand damage. RAG limits the model's action space to pre-approved policy clauses.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q3B: Preventing Demographic Data Leakage**  \n",
    "Data leakage occurs when protected attributes subtly bias GenAI outputs. We prevent this via **Systematic Feature Exclusion** (stripping demographics from the LLM prompt payload entirely) and **Automated Output Validation** (scanning output for demographic leakage prior to delivery)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
